Week 4: Unsupervised Learning & Dimensionality Reduction
📋 Learning Objectives
By the end of this week, you will be able to:

✅ Understand the difference between supervised and unsupervised learning

✅ Implement K-Means clustering for customer segmentation

✅ Use Hierarchical clustering for nested groupings

✅ Apply DBSCAN for density-based clustering

✅ Master Principal Component Analysis (PCA) for dimensionality reduction

✅ Visualize high-dimensional data with t-SNE

✅ Detect anomalies using unsupervised techniques

✅ Evaluate clustering performance with various metrics

✅ Build a complete customer segmentation system
📚 Theory Content

Algorithm	       |   Type	               |   Shape	       |     Pros	                       |     Cons

K-Means	         |   Centroid-based	     |   Spherical	   |     Fast, scalable	             |     Need to choose K, sensitive to outliers

Hierarchical	   |   Connectivity-based	 |   Any	         |     Dendrogram, no K needed	   |     Slow for large data

DBSCAN	         |   Density-based	     |   Arbitrary	   |     Finds outliers, no K needed |	   Varies with density

Gaussian Mixture |	 Distribution-based	 |   Elliptical	   |     Soft assignments	           |     Complex, slow


